The reason that the optical is seen as JKB is that the return device type numeric value in the 
SCSI Inquiry string is 7. For a winchester disk it is 0.

To enable full support under OSF/1 it is necessary to make the optical be seen as a winchester. 
Many of the opticals from IBM, HP etc have an option switch that enables this to happen.

The problem is that even if you create an entry in /usr/sys/data/cam_data.c and rebuild the 
kernel, the optical will still not be configured as the device type is wrong.

The other point to note is that to maintain file system compatibility with the operating system, 
the disk pack used must be 512 bytes/sector.

Mark Woolfson



