The 'Intruder alert' from `whoami` indicates that
getpwuid(geteuid()) failed.  Thus, it looks like that machine's
DCE/SIA setup isn't working right, since the password entry for
that uid is not being found from passwdEtc.

Try this:
	# (umask 077 ; touch /var/adm/sialog)
Then try the `whoami` (from another session).
	# mv /var/adm/sialog /var/adm/sialog.save

Look to see whether the DCE routines were ever called to obtain
the password entry for that uid.

For that matter (first), check /etc/sia/matrix.conf to be sure it
(still) has entries for DCE in it.  (Compare with a working
system if you're not sure.)

