     Hi,

This is a digest of the answers I got to my question about the "dynamic load":

>> I am looking for information on how loading foreign or external code
>> in a running application. (Also called 'dynamic load', 'foreign code load')

It appears now to me that it is possible on (at least) :
SunOS4, SOLARIS, HP-UX, AIX, Unixware, OSF/1

and not possible on ULTRIX


Some tips (which do not replace a look at the man at all...):

- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
On SunOS, SOLARIS, Unixware:     dlopen, dlsym ...

Compile with the -G flag to create a sharable object and link the application
with the dl library.
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
On HP-UX:     shl_load, shl_findsym ...

The code to be loaded has to be compiled in position-independent (+z/+Z) and
linked using ld -b.
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
On AIX:     load, loadbind

Compile the shared object using -bE, -bI ...
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 
On OSF/1:      dlopen, dlsym
- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - 


