In article <3fvd6j$ldp@uuneo.neosoft.com>, thuy@starbase.neosoft.com (Thuy Mai) writes:

>I need disktab entry for Segate ST124 1Gb drive.

Well, actually, you may not.  The disklabel command can get the
geometry and default partition table from the driver.  If the
disk is labeled newfs can get the geometry from there.  The
information in the label is enough for most uses.  If not, you
can work backwards from there to make an entry.

Example:

# disklabel -wr /dev/rrz#c st124
# newfs /dev/rrz#c

