For DEC OSF/1 AXP, you can get this information from its Software Product
Description; the current version is located at:

	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/info/SPD/41-61-08.txt

For your reference, here is the relevant excerpt from the SPD.

 OSF provides an interface for developing portable applications that
 will run on a variety of hardware platforms. DEC OSF/1 is compliant
 with the OSF Application Environment Specification (AES) that spec-
 ifies the interface to support these portable applications. In addi-
 tion, the DEC OSF/1 Operating System complies with standards and in-
 dustry specifications, including X/Open[TM], POSIX[R], FIPS, AT&T[R]
 System V Interface Definition (SVID), and XTI.

 STANDARDS

 X/Open

 DEC OSF/1 conforms to XPG4 at the Base level, and includes support for
 the following areas of the Common Application Environment (CAE) Is-
 sue X/Open 4: System Calls and Libraries, Internationalized Commands
 and Utilities, and C Language. In addition, the Window System Display
 and the Window Application Interface, as well as the optional Digi-
 tal Pascal, Ada, and C++ compilers for DEC OSF/1 conform to XPG4. DEC
 OSF/1 Network File System (NFS) has successfully completed the optional
 XPG4 NFS branding process. The portability, connectivity, and inter-
 operability of software which has obtained the XPG4 NFS brand is en-
 sured. 

 SPEC 1170

 DEC OSF/1 Version 3.0 provides most of the Application Programming In-
 terfaces (with the exception of SVR4 curses) listed in the first draft
 of the Common Operating System Environment specification. Digital is
 committed to fully complying with SPEC 1170 soon after the final spec-
 ification is published.

 SVID

 DEC OSF/1 has been tested using the AT&T System V Verification suite
 and conforms to the Base System as specified in SVID2, and the Base
 System and Kernel Extensions as specified in SVID3 (Volume 1). DEC OSF
 /1 provides more than 400 SVID3/SVR4 compatible commands and inter-
 faces.

 POSIX

 DEC OSF/1 provides all the interfaces required by the IEEE 1003.1-1990
 (also known as ISO/IEC 9945-1:1990) standard. This product is also cer-
 tified with the National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST)
 Federal Information Processing Standards (FIPS) 151-2.

 DEC OSF/1 complies with the IEEE POSIX 1003.2 standard for commands
 and utilities.

 DEC OSF/1 provides many of the interfaces required by the IEEE POSIX
 1003.1b-1993 (formerly 1003.4 Draft 14) standard for realtime.
