Hi Mark

Well, I think that you didn't configure your SLIP interface properly. If you are using
this Protocol, you have also to tell wich Host is your machine and wich Host is on the
other side of the other side of the line. You have to use the ifconfig BEFORE you attach
the line with slattach. 

 ifconfig sl0 XXX.XXX.XXX.XX (your Hostadress) XXX.XXX.XXX.XXX (default Gateway) netmask 255.255.255.0
 slattach tty0 38400

This worked on a DEC 3000-500 running OSF/1 with a analog and a digital (ISDN) Line. 



