Depending on the way the Xresources file is read, it is sometimes piped
through cpp first. This is the case if it's just passed to xrdb. Since
current cpp preprocessors know about C++ and remove c++ comments, as
soon as they see a double slash, they remove the end of the line. What
you should do is either use the -nocpp option of xrdb or use somehow
hide the double slash with quotes:

	http:/\/hello.epgl.ch/

Hope it helps,


	Stefan
