Hi,

In article <weich.789825779@tpdec1> weich@physik.tu-chemnitz.de (Frank Weich) writes:

   As a HP JetDirect netinterface is built in we want to use it :-)
   But HP just supports HP-UX, Solaris and SunOS for the printer-server 
   (and we have none of these) - so the question is quite clear: 

   What to do? Has anybody sucessfully installed printer service under
   OSF/1 (especially to the HP JetDirect netinterface) ?

I have. You don't need special software. The JetDirect interface has
an ethernet connector, so we used it. The printer can be set up either
manually using telnet, or automatically by using the internet boot
protocol (by creating an entry in /etc/bootptab). You also need to
create a printer entry in /etc/printcap. Specifically, set the rm
(remote) directive to the printer name. If all goes well, lpd will now
send its files directly to the remote printer. This procedure is
described in the configuration guide.

cheers,

Eric
