We noticed this begining to happen shortly after we'd finished the initial 
installs for a number of DEC 3000/300X's last Summer.  We were running OSF/1,
v. 2.0 at the time.  I noticed this happening after a dump had terminated
abnormally and a check by out sales rep. resulted in DEC notifying us that 
there was a problem in dump/rdump where if it was executed from cron and the
the dump failed for any reason it would die ... and in the process it would
also kill its parent (cron).  

It was tracked to the file /usr/sys/opt/DNABASE200/osi_transport.o - we received
a patched version which solved the problem.  When we upgraded to OSF/1, v. 2.1
we were told that this bug was supposedly fixed but we ended up reinstalling
the patch as we found the problem still manifested itself.

Your DEC Rep. should be able to get their engineering dept. to send you a copy
of the patched version of osi_transport.o.  I've been informed (again) that 
this is now fixed in 3.0........


