To the woman from DEC that responded to this post - (Sorry, I accidentally
deleted your reply from my email):

Yes the drive was plenty clean...because we had a backup tape hammered a 
couple of months ago by a tar to the wrong device we leave the stacker 
unloaded and in "manual" mode.  The tape is mounted just prior to the backup
kicking off; sometimes NSR rejects the tape out of hand and goes on to the next
sequential volume, sometimes it writes on the mounted tape for a minute or so
and then goes on to the next sequential volume...there's no real pattern to 
this problem. And since this is a relatively new installation all of the tapes
are brand new so that can be ruled out also.

Over the weekend it wanted to write on a tape that was 3 volumes old (and still
had a few mb. available on it)...it wrote to that tape first, still didn't 
fill the index and went on to the volume that it should have started with in 
the first place.  This out-of-seq. issue doesn't happen all the time...its
rather haphazard and even tho' its infrequent it annoying because the indexes
get all out of sequence.

