Brian,

Listed below is an example program of how to get the information you
need.  I haven't figured out if there's any way to get the destination
service name.  You might want that if you had more than one service
defined on the system and wanted to know which one a user had connected
to.  I originally got parts of this example from DEC through DSNLink, so
I guess I should give them some credit too. (The DSNLink people are
sometimes VERY helpful).  As far as I know, this stuff isn't documented
anywhere.

ALSO NOTE: Since LAT was completely re-implemented in OSF/1 V3.0, you
have to use different code for OSF/1 V2.0.  THIS CODE WILL ONLY WORK
FOR V3.0 OSF/1.  I have the 2.0 code if anyone needs it.

Hope this helps.


Here's the code :

/*
** Get LAT connection information
**
** This code is for OSF/1 V3.0 ONLY
**
** Written by someone at Digital Equipment Corporation
**
** Adapted by Sam Eads (HBO & Company, Atlanta, GA, U.S.A)
*/

#include        <stropts.h>
#include        <lat/streams/latioc.h>
#include        <sys/fcntl.h>
#include        <sys/stat.h>
struct  stat    statb;


main(agc,arg)
int agc;
char **arg;
{
        int tfd;
        lats_info latioctl_port;
        struct strioctl strioctl;

        tfd = open("/dev/streams/lat",O_RDWR);
        if(tfd < 0) {
                perror("openning /dev/streams/lat");
                exit(0);
                }
        if(fstat(0,&statb) < 0) {
                perror("stating fd 0");
                exit(0);
                }
        bzero(&latioctl_port,sizeof(lats_info));
        latioctl_port.info_dev = minor(statb.st_rdev);
        strioctl.ic_cmd = LIOC_INFO_SHOW;
        strioctl.ic_len = sizeof(lats_info);
        strioctl.ic_dp = (char *)&latioctl_port;
        if(ioctl(tfd,I_STR,&strioctl) < 0) {
                perror("on latioctl call");
                exit(0);
                }
        close(tfd);
        printf("lcl_svc=%s\n",latioctl_port.lcl_service);
        printf("lcl_por=%s\n",latioctl_port.lcl_port);
        printf("rmt_svc=%s\n",latioctl_port.rmt_service);
        printf("rmt_por=%s\n",latioctl_port.rmt_port);
        printf("rmt_ond=%s\n",latioctl_port.rmt_node);
}


