:   If you have all three, then things should work. The first item is easy -
: load code for a given server is independent of the host OS. So, a PRO801ENG.
: SYS (the DECserver 200 load code) file from any OS should work on any other
: OS (though you may have to rename it to lower case, remove the .SYS part,
: etc.).

:   The second item should come with the operating system for multi-user sys-
: tems from DEC (for PC's it comes with the load image kit). I would assume
: that DEC's OSF/1 includes MOP, but I can't say for sure. Likewise for the
: third item.


The MOP loader is available with the DECnet subset.  Support for incoming
LAT connections on OSF/1 is available.  Make sure you have the LAT subset 
loaded and LAT built into the kernel.  For a quick setup, run latsetup
and specify the number of incoming connections (gettys) that you wish to
offer. 

By all means, read the "lat_intro", "latcp" and "latsetup" man pages.


