>
> 2. Because I don't know the load on the network and on the machines,
>    you can try to increase the timeout option for the specific nfs
>    mount (either in the command line or in /etc/fstab)

With regard to Item #2, the filesystem is not NFS-mounted in the
"traditional" way; that is, not hard-mounted via an entry in
/etc/fstab.  Rather, like all exported filesystems at our site, it is
mounted on-demand via the automounter.  I double-checked the manpage on
automount, and found that on OSF/1 the default timeout for unused
filesystems (like during linkage) is 5 minutes.  I ran an experiment,
and found that the time from the start of linking until the NFS write
error 60 occurs is only 50 seconds.

So, that leaves Item #1.  I am not particularly pleased with the idea
of upgrading to a different version of the O/S, especially because the
problem does not occur on any other of the project hosts, all running the
same version of OSF/1.

